{"abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Plugin Architecture","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Core-Middleware","text":"Core Middleware","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"action-agnostic infrastructure"}]},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" needs keypaths to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" properties."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" needs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" so it can snapshot and compare."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Domain-Plugins","text":"Domain Plugins","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain-specific modules"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Comparison","text":"Comparison","type":"heading"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action knowledge"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lifecycle hooks"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns effects"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State coupling"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wiring"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Target"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","text":"The Decision Rule"},{"name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"yes"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"important"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","text":"Hook Selection Guide","type":"heading"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Capture state "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Handle domain-specific actions "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Observe state "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits."}]}]}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Registration-Order","text":"Registration Order","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Next-Steps","text":"Next Steps","type":"heading"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware"}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Plugins","title":"Plugins","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","kind":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Persistence Middleware","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"title":"UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"title":"PluginHost","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"title":"EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI with built-in persistence."}],"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"type":"topic","title":"SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"title":"Building a Domain Plugin","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","type":"topic"}}}